# Accuracy of trapezoid, Simpson and 4-node Gauss-Legendre rules on [0, 1]

Composite rules, n = 2^k panels of width 1/n, k = 1..10 (trapezoid: 1 interval per panel; Simpson: endpoints and midpoint per panel (2n subintervals); Gauss: 4 nodes per panel), on exp(-x^2) (smooth) and x^(1/3) (singular at 0). Float64 absolute errors vs `mpmath.quad` references (`mp.dps = 40`, mpmath 1.4.1 from PyPI), from a `local-compute` job (`results/errors.csv`).

## References (mpmath 1.4.1, 40 digits)

| function | reference value on [0, 1] |
|---|---|
| exp(-x^2) | 0.7468241328124270253994674361318530053545 |
| x^(1/3) | 0.75 |

## Fitted convergence order

Order = minus the slope of log(error) vs log(n) over points with error > 1e-14.

| function | trapezoid | Simpson | Gauss-Legendre 4 |
|---|---|---|---|
| exp(-x^2) | 2.0008 (10 pts) | 3.9970 (8 pts) | 8.2358 (2 pts)* |
| x^(1/3) | 1.3246 (10 pts) | 1.3333 (10 pts) | 1.3333 (10 pts) |

\* two-point estimate, no residual degrees of freedom; insufficient to establish asymptotic behavior.

